      "writtenOn": "2023-03-09T17:32:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should we remove this? I think with the whole series we are adding cpu_capacity_inverted so probably just put it into one of ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE so the size of the struct rq stays same?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1088,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1088,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "546b12fed19982d354e86cc384108b9d720e16eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0224ca74_c0b8f94b",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/sched.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1088,
      "author": {
        "id": 1976445
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-09T18:48:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE is 8 bytes. unsigned long is 4 bytes. Hence the additional reserve.",
      "parentUuid": "244eb3f5_4b2c4974",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1088,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1088,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "546b12fed19982d354e86cc384108b9d720e16eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b95097b8_4f50c339",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/sched.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1088,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T09:03:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e unsigned long is 4 bytes\n\nWell, it\u0027s definitely 8 bytes 😊\n\nAnd fwiw using reserved slots should done using the dedicated macro (`ANDROID_KABI_USE()` or something like that IIRC), to avoid CRC issues and whatnot. But you really shouldn\u0027t need this anyway, those slots are reserved to fixup LTS merges.",
      "parentUuid": "0224ca74_c0b8f94b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1088,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1088,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "546b12fed19982d354e86cc384108b9d720e16eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fae6452f_68243fd5",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/sched.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1088,
      "author": {
        "id": 1976445
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T12:38:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. I got too lazy to write a test code and checked the ABI table which said 32bits; but I can see above it now it says long is 64bits\n\nhttps://developer.arm.com/documentation/den0024/a/Porting-to-A64/Data-types\n\n\u003e But you really shouldn\u0027t need this anyway, those slots are reserved to fixup LTS merges.\n\nGot it. Next time might be easier to just flag the potential breakage only then.",
      "parentUuid": "b95097b8_4f50c339",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1088,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1088,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "546b12fed19982d354e86cc384108b9d720e16eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
