      "writtenOn": "2023-03-09T08:21:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a quick note, we had things like this in the past, and given that struct rq is by definition per-cpu, the easiest solution to not touch the ABI was to move the new fields to a dedicated per-cpu variable, and leave struct rq alone...",
      "parentUuid": "42cbffad_26b301f8",
      "revId": "546b12fed19982d354e86cc384108b9d720e16eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
